{
  "id": "COMPOUND:18973 - PROTEIN:5673",
  "verbalization": "Arborescidine D appears to exert its biological effects through a shared target, Protein-tyrosine phosphatase LC-PTP, which is inhibited by multiple compounds, including [(3S,10S,13R,17R)-17-(5-ethyl-6-methylhept-6-en-2-yl)-4,10,13,14-tetramethyl-1,2,3,4,5,6,9,11,12,15,16,17-dodecahydrocyclopenta[a]phenanthren-3-yl] acetate, Methyl 3,4-Dihydroxy-5-Methoxybenzoate, and 2-Nonyl-4-hydroxyquinoline N-oxide. These compounds all act as inhibitors of the same target, suggesting a common mechanism of action. The evidence supports a potential role for Arborescidine D in modulating the activity of Protein-tyrosine phosphatase LC-PTP, which may influence the function of LS174T, a cellular target. The high scores in the evidence suggest a strong, consistent relationship between Arborescidine D and LS174T, likely through the inhibition of the shared target. The mechanism is supported by multiple independent pathways, reinforcing the likelihood of a direct or indirect interaction between Arborescidine D and LS174T.",
